---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Map">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>The map</h1>
    <p class="intro">Not built yet. The map is planned as the second phase of the site.</p>
    <h2>What it will show</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Who owned every location in Iberia and the Maghreb at each checkpoint, with a slider like the realm page.</li>
      <li>Where battles and sieges were fought, linked to their wars.</li>
      <li>Arabic place names from the gazetteer, with the game's names on hover.</li>
      <li>Later, the colonies.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What it needs</h2>
    <p>
      The game's own map files from the gaming PC: the location bitmap and the location definitions. A tool in
      <code>tools/</code> will turn them into shapes the site can draw, once, and then colour them from each
      checkpoint's ownership data.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro { font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink-2); }
  li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  code { font-size: 0.9em; }
</style>
